# Security headers for everything the api Worker serves from static assets: the shell, its SPA fallback, JS/CSS,
# the manifest and the service worker (ADR 0001 decision 8, #118). Cloudflare's assets layer applies this file,
# in production and in `wrangler dev` alike; it is never served itself. Responses the Worker code builds (/api/*)
# are not covered by it.
#
# - script-src 'self': the build has no inline script (inlineCritical is off in apps/console/project.json) and no eval.
# - style-src 'unsafe-inline': Angular injects component styles as <style> elements at runtime; a nonce would need a
#   per-request shell rendered by the Worker on every navigation. No script can be injected through it.
# - connect-src 'self': the app and the service worker only call this origin (/api/v1, ngsw.json, assets).
# - The OAuth connect leaves for github.com by a top-level navigation (location.assign), which CSP does not limit;
#   form-action 'self' only covers form submissions, and the app's forms never navigate.
# - frame-src: the outer bound for the Designs and Demo frames (#20), the free-tier homes of Storybook and
#   design pages. The exact gate is GET /api/v1/projects/:slug/embed-origins, which the app checks before it
#   renders a frame. No 'self': the console never frames itself, and a same-origin frame with allow-scripts +
#   allow-same-origin could lift its own sandbox.
# - frame-ancestors 'none' + X-Frame-Options: DENY: nobody may frame the console (clickjacking on one-tap answers).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-src https://*.pages.dev https://*.workers.dev https://*.github.io; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin

# Version metadata is never kept stale (#306): the service worker decides about updates from ngsw.json, the browser
# about the worker from ngsw-worker.js (and safety-worker.js, the kill switch), and every page from the shell.
# no-cache = store, but ask the origin before every reuse. Hashed files keep the assets layer's default.
# Rules match the request path, so the shell needs one per place it is answered: `/` (/index.html redirects there)
# and each client-side route of apps/console/src/app/app.routes.ts (the SPA fallback; pwa.spec.ts keeps them in step).
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/p/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/needs-you
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/overview
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/settings
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/settings/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/ngsw.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/ngsw-worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/safety-worker.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
